# Opinion

Meeting: 0005-investigate-ssl-error-for-rps-arena-deployment
Agent: Developer
Task: Investigate SSL error for RPS Arena deployment
Context:
  - User reported ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR when browsing the Azure App Service host; pipeline claims success.
  - Curl via the provided proxy returns HTTP 403 from the proxy tunnel, so the env cannot validate the public endpoint directly.
  - Server bootstrap previously awaited MongoDB unconditionally when MONGODB_URI was set; failures would prevent the process from starting.
  - Azure containers workflow tests failed because healthCheckPath entries drifted.
Position:
  - Likely root cause for “invalid response” is the app process not starting (e.g., failing MongoDB connection) leading Azure to return TLS errors/502s.
  - Proxy restrictions in this environment prevent verifying the live site, but logs plus workflow signals point to runtime crash risk when Mongo is unreachable.
Recommendations:
  - Make bootstrap resilient: attempt MongoDB, log failures, but fall back to the in-memory store so the app still responds.
  - Keep JSON response handling reusable to reduce duplication in server routes.
  - Restore healthCheckPath settings in the Azure container workflow to keep deployments green and App Service health probes correct.
